Experienced hackers often KICK bees.  They don't have a lot of hit
points, and they move too fast to run away from, so....

The flyswatter idea might be a good one for a new weapon.  It only
does 1 (or maybe 1-2) points of damage, but it has a +5 bonus to hit
insects and arachnids (bees, assorted spiders, scorpions, bugbears, etc.).

Or maybe some "bug bomb" tool.  When you apply it, all the bugs in the
room take damage.  

Or maybe smashing a potion of poison in a room will damage all the
monsters in the room.  Sure, this will affect you also, but with a
roomful of bugs it will take out a lot of them.

Of course, we can't make beehives too easy.  One of these couldn't
affect the whole room.  Perhaps just a limited area....

